# Protected Odoo User Accounts

Never modify personal Odoo user accounts or existing administrator accounts for testing.

## Off-limits (unless explicitly instructed)

- Dirk Visagie (`visagiedl@gmail.com`, user #2)
- Brent Petersen (`brent@petsempire.co.za`, user #5)
- Any other existing production or development user

## Forbidden actions on existing users

- Setting or resetting passwords via `odoo shell`, RPC, or UI automation
- `user.password = ...`, `new_password`, `_set_password`, `action_reset_password`
- Creating temporary password-reset helper scripts targeting existing users

## Required approach for login/auth testing

1. Create or reuse a dedicated test user with an obvious name (e.g. **Cursor Test**, **POS Test User**, **Development Test**).
2. Assign only the minimum groups required for the feature under test.
3. Password changes on the test user are allowed during testing.
4. If admin permissions are needed, create a dedicated **Test Administrator** account — do not use real admin accounts.

## End-of-task reporting

Report:

- Which test user was used
- Any password changes made to the test user
- Any temporary scripts or helper files created

## Cleanup

Delete temporary helper scripts (e.g. password reset scripts) when testing is complete unless the user asks to keep them.

Treat user authentication and credentials as protected.
